    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41091" root="هرا" body-key="h">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَهْرُوْءٌ</span></b> , from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هُرِئَ</span>, pl. with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ون</span>, [in the CK, for
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَهْرُوؤُونَ</span> is put <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَهْرَؤُنَ</span>,] <i>Perishing of cold,</i> or <i>heat.</i>
(Ks, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Explained by AHn [in his book on
plants] by the words <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَلَّذِى قَدْ أَنْضَجَهُ البَرْدُ</span>
[meaning, What is <i>nipped, shrunk, shrivelled,</i> or
<i>blasted, by the cold:</i> see art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نضج</span>]. (TA.)

